# Catalyst Center connection
#
# The YAML config file is OPTIONAL. Exporting these env vars (or putting them in
# a .env next to where you run the command) is enough to start the server — which
# is what makes it work under `uv tool install` + an MCP client, whose working
# directory is not your project dir.
#
# Precedence (highest first): CLI flags > env vars > YAML file > built-in defaults.
#
# DevNet always-on sandbox: https://devnetsandbox.cisco.com/
# Sandbox host: sandboxdnac.cisco.com  (creds rotate — verify on the sandbox page)
CATALYST_CENTER_USERNAME=
CATALYST_CENTER_PASSWORD=

# Optional — override host/port without editing any YAML.
# Defaults: host=sandboxdnac.cisco.com, port=443, verify_ssl=true.
# CATALYST_CENTER_HOST=sandboxdnac.cisco.com
# CATALYST_CENTER_PORT=443
#
# TLS: keep verification ENABLED (the default). If your controller uses a
# self-signed or private-CA certificate, point at a CA bundle so the cert chain
# is still verified — do NOT disable verification, which would expose your
# device credentials and X-Auth-Token to man-in-the-middle interception.
#   export SSL_CERT_FILE=/path/to/your-ca-bundle.pem
# Disabling verification (CATALYST_CENTER_VERIFY_SSL=false) is a last resort and
# emits a startup WARNING on stderr.

# MCP server transport bearer token (only used when transport.auth.type=bearer)
# CATALYST_CENTER_MCP_TOKEN=
